{
  "title": "Stride-duration decile asymmetry: uncertain Parkinson prediction transfer and fragile measurement stability",
  "abstract": "Stride-duration decile asymmetry reduced exploratory cross-collection logloss by 0.025206, but the joint-bootstrap95% interval for augmented-minus-baseline loss was [-0.11095589524249512, 0.025898702917356575]. Weak target split-window stability and reversal at20ms rounding prevent a claim of a reliable superior Parkinson marker.",
